int l = 0, r = n;

while (l < r) {
    int m = l + (r - l) / 2;
    if (arr[m] < target) l = m + 1;
    else r = m;
}

if (l < n && arr[l] == target) {
    return l;
}

return -1;
```

Comment: Loop ends with `l` equal to the first where `arr[l] >= target`, i.e. `l == lower_bound(target)`.

